---
title: Anseriformes
---
# Anseriformes

Anseriformes is the order of waterfowl, holding the ducks, geese and swans of
[[anatidae]] together with the screamers and the magpie goose. The bill carries
lamellae along its edges that strain food from water, and the young are
precocial, leaving for the water within a day of hatching. The order is one of
the two oldest lineages of modern birds, alongside the gamebirds.
